<title>JAPAN: DAIHYAKU LIFE HAS UNREALISED LOSSES ON SECURITIES.</title>
<headline>DAIHYAKU LIFE HAS UNREALISED LOSSES ON SECURITIES.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daihyaku Mutual Life Insurance Co said on Tuesday that it had 1.57 billion yen in unrealised losses on securities holdings at the end of March against a profit of 79.13 billion yen a year earlier.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the securities include domestic bonds, stocks and foreign securities.</p>
<p>As for shareholdings, Daihyaku said it had 12.06 billion yen in unrealised profits on shareholdings at the end of March, down from 94.10 billion yen a year earlier.</p>
</text>
